/E (       Although global music streaming revenue continues to grow, recent growth rates have slowed relative to earlier expansion phases, reinforcing signals of category maturity. In such environments, competitive advantage shifts away from acquisition-driven growth toward retention, habit strength, and perceived indispensability within everyday routines. What this implies is that the free-to-premium path is most effective when premium is experienced as protection of routines \(no interruption, more control\) rather than as an abstract upgrade.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
