/E (       When artists withdraw content due to ethical, political, or compensation-related concerns, impact concentrates among high-involvement fandoms and subcultures. These groups can dropout  collectively, and such loss reduces perceived completeness and cultural relevance. This risk is tightly tied to live events and niche communities where artist access drives both online behavior and offline participation. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
